        }
      ],
      "impact": "The galvanic isolation between the logic side and the CAN bus side is defeated, allowing ground loops and losing the protective isolation intended for the CAN interfaces.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["D14", "D23", "D4"],
      "pins": ["D14.2", "D23.2", "D4.2"],
      "nets": ["/LED_3.3V_POWER_SW"],
      "observed": "The anodes of D14, D23, and D4 are tied together on net /LED_3.3V_POWER_SW, but this net has no connection to any supply or driver.",
      "expected": "The LED anodes should be connected to a 3.3V supply (e.g., +3V3 or a switched 3.3V rail) to allow the LEDs to illuminate.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/LED_3.3V_POWER_SW : D14.2(A,passive) D23.2(A,passive) D4.2(A,passive)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "D14 (Ethernet LED), D23 (Ethernet LED), and D4 (activity LED) will never light, disabling their indicator functions.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["R60", "D30"],
      "pins": ["R60.2", "D30.2", "D30.4"],
      "nets": ["ESTOP_OUT", "Net-(D30-K2)"],
      "observed": "R60 pin 2 is on ESTOP_OUT, and D30 pin 4 (A2) is also on ESTOP_OUT. R60 pin 1 connects to D30 pin 2 (K2) on Net-(D30-K2). This places R60 in parallel with the LED between ESTOP_OUT and a floating node.",
      "expected": "R60 should connect the cathode of D30's second LED to GND (or a return) to complete the current path, typically as a current-limiting resistor to ground.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "ESTOP_OUT : D30.4(A2,input) J13.6(Pin_6,passive) J2.6(Pin_6,passive) R60.2(passive) U36.4(Y,output)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "Net-(D30-K2) : D30.2(K2,input) R60.1(passive)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The second LED in D30 (likely an e-stop indicator) will never light, and ESTOP_OUT does not have the intended LED load.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain three anomalies: the isolated CAN transceivers have their logic and bus grounds tied together, defeating isolation; the anodes of D14, D23, and D4 are on a floating net with no supply; and R60 is miswired so D30's second LED has no return path to ground."
}

